WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.355 --> 00:00:02.114
This is the Taxes page.

2
00:00:02.114 --> 00:00:05.193
It works out your realized gains and cost basis from

3
00:00:05.193 --> 00:00:08.390
the trades and transfers on your connected exchanges.

4
00:00:09.054 --> 00:00:12.860
Cost basis is what you paid for a coin, including fees.

5
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.215
When you sell, the difference between what you received

6
00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:19.203
and what you paid is your realized gain or loss.

7
00:00:19.203 --> 00:00:23.871
Cyrus replays your whole history to work that out, sale by sale.

8
00:00:24.543 --> 00:00:29.624
At the top is your trade history, one card for each exchange account, showing

9
00:00:29.624 --> 00:00:34.573
how many trades Cyrus has stored, when it last synced, and a status badge.

10
00:00:35.242 --> 00:00:38.091
Up to date means the full history is in.

11
00:00:38.091 --> 00:00:44.181
Partly synced means Cyrus is still working back through it, so the figures may be incomplete.

12
00:00:44.181 --> 00:00:50.471
Needs permission means the API key can't read trade history, and the card says what to change.

13
00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:52.941
Some exchanges have limits.

14
00:00:52.941 --> 00:00:57.489
Binance and Gemini only report trades one market at a time, so Cyrus

15
00:00:57.489 --> 00:01:01.970
checks the markets for coins you hold, have moved, or have traded.

16
00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:08.100
Robinhood has no record of individual fills, so each filled order counts as one trade.

17
00:01:08.787 --> 00:01:12.221
Your first visit syncs anything Cyrus hasn't seen.

18
00:01:12.221 --> 00:01:17.897
After that, Sync history fetches new trades from every exchange, then your deposits and

19
00:01:17.897 --> 00:01:23.311
withdrawals, because a move between your own exchanges carries cost basis with it.

20
00:01:24.004 --> 00:01:26.560
Realized gains covers one tax year.

21
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.217
First, choose how Cyrus decides which coins you sold.

22
00:01:30.217 --> 00:01:35.949
FIFO, first in, first out, treats your oldest coins as sold first.

23
00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:40.741
HIFO, highest in, first out, treats your most expensive

24
00:01:40.741 --> 00:01:44.986
coins as sold first, which usually means a smaller gain.

25
00:01:44.986 --> 00:01:46.675
Watch the figures change.

26
00:01:47.371 --> 00:01:50.193
Cyrus remembers your choice for next time.

27
00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:51.922
Let's switch back to FIFO.

28
00:01:52.597 --> 00:01:57.627
The year menu lists every year you've sold something in, plus the current one.

29
00:01:57.627 --> 00:01:59.981
Here's last year, and back to this one.

30
00:01:59.981 --> 00:02:03.544
Dates are in universal time, matching the export.

31
00:02:04.221 --> 00:02:05.740
The tiles add up the year.

32
00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:10.525
Net gain or loss is the total, split into short term, for coins held

33
00:02:10.525 --> 00:02:15.168
one year or less, and long term, for coins held more than a year.

34
00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.402
The two are often taxed differently.

35
00:02:18.095 --> 00:02:22.207
Proceeds is what your sales brought in, valued in US dollars at

36
00:02:22.207 --> 00:02:26.449
the time of each trade, and cost basis is what those coins cost.

37
00:02:26.449 --> 00:02:32.221
Dollars and dollar stablecoins count as cash, so they never make a gain or a loss.

38
00:02:32.882 --> 00:02:39.374
The table lists every sale: the coin and amount, when it was bought and sold, the proceeds,

39
00:02:39.374 --> 00:02:45.438
cost, and gain or loss, whether it was short or long term, and the exchange account.

40
00:02:46.119 --> 00:02:50.365
One sale can span several rows when it used coins bought at different

41
00:02:50.365 --> 00:02:53.689
times, since each purchase has its own cost and date.

42
00:02:53.689 --> 00:02:57.359
Swapping one coin for another counts as selling the first.

43
00:02:57.359 --> 00:03:03.556
And a fee paid in a third coin, like BNB on Binance, counts as a small sale of that coin.

44
00:03:04.228 --> 00:03:08.455
Cyrus tracks your coins separately for each exchange account, because a

45
00:03:08.455 --> 00:03:12.742
coin bought on Kraken can't be sold on Binance until you move it there.

46
00:03:12.742 --> 00:03:16.532
Sending coins out of an exchange isn't counted as a sale.

47
00:03:17.216 --> 00:03:22.801
When you move coins between two of your connected exchanges, and the transfer is matched, they

48
00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:28.030
keep their original cost and purchase date, and the network fee is added to their cost.

49
00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:31.581
That's why confirming matches on the Transfers page matters.

50
00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.575
Sometimes Cyrus can't know what you paid.

51
00:03:34.575 --> 00:03:39.059
If coins arrived from outside your connected exchanges, or you sold more

52
00:03:39.059 --> 00:03:43.605
than your history covers, the cost is marked missing instead of guessed.

53
00:03:44.282 --> 00:03:47.661
Those sales still count toward proceeds but are left out of

54
00:03:47.661 --> 00:03:51.041
the gain, and the net gain tile says how many are missing.

55
00:03:51.041 --> 00:03:54.533
Check before filing lists what needs attention, like

56
00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:57.689
these two thousand ADA deposited from outside.

57
00:03:58.364 --> 00:04:03.859
Needs info narrows the table to just the sales missing a cost or a dollar price.

58
00:04:03.859 --> 00:04:08.793
The totals still cover the whole year, so you can watch them change as you fill things in.

59
00:04:09.477 --> 00:04:11.595
To fill a gap, click Fix.

60
00:04:11.595 --> 00:04:15.334
For coins deposited from outside, enter what you originally

61
00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:19.201
paid in total, including fees, and the date you bought them.

62
00:04:19.882 --> 00:04:23.124
The purchase date decides short or long term, so use

63
00:04:23.124 --> 00:04:26.242
when you bought the coins, not when they arrived.

64
00:04:26.242 --> 00:04:32.345
For several purchases, enter the total cost and the most recent date, the cautious choice.

65
00:04:32.345 --> 00:04:35.484
As you type, Cyrus shows the cost per coin.

66
00:04:36.174 --> 00:04:38.278
Other gaps get their own forms.

67
00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:42.501
A sale with no purchase history asks for the purchase it came from, and

68
00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:46.842
a trade priced in another coin asks what that coin was worth in dollars.

69
00:04:46.842 --> 00:04:48.159
We'll cancel this one.

70
00:04:48.835 --> 00:04:51.830
Entered by hand collects everything you've filled in.

71
00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:57.164
Each entry feeds every figure above, is marked as entered manually

72
00:04:57.164 --> 00:05:01.285
in the Form 8949 export, and can be removed later.

73
00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:05.950
Add a purchase records coins Cyrus never saw, like ones bought

74
00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.804
before an exchange's records begin, or on another platform.

75
00:05:09.804 --> 00:05:15.375
Pick the exchange account, the coin, the amount, the total cost and the date.

76
00:05:15.375 --> 00:05:17.596
It counts toward sales on that account.

77
00:05:18.274 --> 00:05:20.033
When you're ready, export.

78
00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:26.136
Form 8949 CSV gives one row per sale for the selected year and method, in the

79
00:05:26.136 --> 00:05:32.240
columns of the IRS form, with a note on anything missing or entered by hand.

80
00:05:32.916 --> 00:05:37.835
Koinly CSV exports every trade and transfer in your full history,

81
00:05:37.835 --> 00:05:42.906
in Koinly's universal import format, to import as a single wallet.

82
00:05:42.906 --> 00:05:49.129
Moves between your own exchanges are left out, since inside one wallet they'd only be noise.

83
00:05:49.798 --> 00:05:53.338
As the note at the bottom says, this isn't tax advice.

84
00:05:53.338 --> 00:05:58.338
Cyrus's figures are a starting point, worked out from the history it could fetch.

85
00:05:58.338 --> 00:06:03.777
Review them, and your export, with your tax software or an accountant before you file.

86
00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.099
That's the Taxes page.

87
00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:08.925
Keep your history synced, fill in what's missing, and

88
00:06:08.925 --> 00:06:11.644
your numbers will be ready whenever you need them.

